{#-
  Tells the operator that a delegate passed a module and no clinical lead
  was sent the certificate: the delegate's site has no lead, the lead has
  no address, or the delegate belongs to no site. So somebody can name a
  lead, or send the certificate on.

  Who and where, never the result. The score and the certificate stay in
  Quill. Context:
    username      the delegate's username
    module_title  the module they passed
    organisation  the organisation that served it
    site          their site's name, or None when they belong to none
    reason        why nobody was told, in words
    url           where to put it right: the site's admin page, or the
                  delegate's when there is no site
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}
{% block subject %}No clinical lead was told that {{ username }} passed{% endblock subject %}
{% block preheader %}{{ reason }}{% endblock preheader %}
{% block body %}
{{ c.heading("No clinical lead *was told*") }}
{{ c.paragraph(username ~ " has passed " ~ module_title ~ " at " ~ organisation ~ ", and no clinical lead was sent the certificate.") }}
{{ c.paragraph("Site: " ~ (site if site else "none")) }}
{{ c.paragraph("Why: " ~ reason) }}
{{ c.button("Put it right", url) }}
{% endblock body %}
{% block reason %}You are receiving this because this address is set to be told when a pass reaches no clinical lead on Quill.{% endblock reason %}

{% block text %}
{{ username }} has passed {{ module_title }} at {{ organisation }}, and no clinical lead was sent the certificate.

Site: {{ site if site else "none" }}
Why: {{ reason }}

Put it right: {{ url }}
{% endblock text %}
